  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Setswana tells time with ordinal hours: hours are now 'ya ntlha', 'ya bobedi' … 'ya lesome le bobedi' and pattern 0 is 'ura {h}' ('ura ya bone' = four o'clock). 'le halofo' (half past) and 'le kotara' (quarter past) are standard; other minutes are additive 'le metsotso e le <n>' (class-4 concord: 'e metlhano' for five). No 'to' phrases: I am not sure of the idiom, additive is always understood. Doubt: 'ya ntlha' vs informal 'ya bongwe' for one o'clock."
    }
  ]
